#import "segmented_control"

// Laws for laying out segmented controls. Each states the expected behavior
// independently of the implementation; `ziran check` proves it over every
// listed input. An implementation edit may not change this file.

// A segment moves to a new row only when wrapping is on, the row already
// holds something, and the segment does not fit.
#law WrapRule forall wrap: 0..1, row: 0..3, next: 0..6, available: 0..6 => SegmentedShouldWrap(wrap != 0, row, next, available) == (wrap != 0 && row > 0 && next > available);
